  "body": "As discussed with @annevk on IRC. (thanks again for the direction)\r\n\r\nCurrently Chrome and IE (but not Firefox) expose `e.total` on `ProgressEvent`s. This was discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/284. \r\n\r\nThe value of `Content-Length` is very valuable on `HEAD` requests. We sometimes make `HEAD` requests to resources in order to choose whether or not they are prohibitively expensive for the client to download or not - or to make smart decisions about downloading them.\r\n\r\nCurrently this is possible (due to `ProgressEvent`s on Chrome) but not Firefox - I think we should safelist the `Content-Length` header in CORS requests.\r\n\r\n",
